{"slug": "octopus-galician-style", "nyt_id": 10835, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10835-octopus-galician-style", "name": "Octopus, Galician Style", "author": "Mark Bittman", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 to 8 servings", "min": 4, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 120, "raw": {"total": "2 hours"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 octopus, about 3 pounds", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "octopus", "preparation": "about 3 pounds", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "Coarse salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "coarse salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "4 medium to large potatoes", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium to large potatoes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "Smoked pimentón", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "smoked pimentón", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Thaw octopus if necessary, either for 24 hours in refrigerator, or for a few hours in a couple of changes of cold water. With a scissors, remove skinny tips of tentacles and, cutting through webbing that connects them, separate the 8 tentacles and discard head. (Alternatively, you can cook the octopus whole and cut it up after cooking.)"}, {"position": 2, "text": "Bring a large pot of water to a boil and salt it well. Put octopus in water and, when it returns to boil, cover and adjust heat so water simmers gently. Cook an hour or so, until octopus is tender. Meanwhile peel potatoes and cut into 2-inch slices. Lower them into water and cook until tender, about a half hour. Remove if they're done before octopus, and keep warm."}, {"position": 3, "text": "When octopus is tender, remove it and drain. Put potatoes on a platter and cut octopus into pieces (again, a scissors is easiest); top potatoes with it. Drizzle all liberally with pimentón, olive oil and coarse salt, and serve hot or warm."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 445.6, "protein_g": 39.5, "carbohydrates_g": 50.6, "fat_g": 9.6, "saturated_fat_g": 1.6, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 108.9, "sodium_mg": 1125.4, "fiber_g": 6.8, "sugar_g": 2.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 6.8, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["spanish"], "diet": ["dairy-free", "gluten-free"], "course": ["main course"], "meal": ["dinner"], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "five ingredient", "octopus", "potato"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/08/dining/octopus-still/octopus-still-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 126}, "video_url": "https://www.nytimes.com/video/dining/1194817092096/octopus-galician-style.html", "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2008-03-05", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:51:40.467595+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "octopus-salad-with-crispy-vegetables", "nyt_id": 7373, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/7373-octopus-salad-with-crispy-vegetables", "name": "Octopus Salad With Crispy Vegetables", "author": "Mark Bittman", "description": "Mark Bittman", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 90, "raw": {"total": "1 1/2 to 2 hours (90 - 120 minutes) plus 3 to 4 hours' marinating and cooling"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "6 medium carrots, peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium carrots", "preparation": "peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "4 small red onions, peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "small red onions", "preparation": "peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 medium celeriac, trimmed and peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "medium celeriac", "preparation": "trimmed and peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 bay leaf", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "bay leaf", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 tablespoon black peppercorns", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "black peppercorns", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 cup white vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "white vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "2 pounds octopus", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "octopus", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "½ cup extra virgin olive oil, or more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": "or more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "Juice of 1 lemon, or more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "juice of 1 lemon", "preparation": "or more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground black pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Hot red pepper flakes", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "hot red pepper flakes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 cup chopped basil, plus more for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped basil", "preparation": "plus more for garnish", "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "5 red bliss potatoes", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "red bliss potatoes", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Roughly chop half the carrots, onions and celeriac, and combine in saucepan with bay leaf, peppercorns and white vinegar. Bring to boil, and add octopus, along with water to cover; cook at least 1 hour, or until octopus is tender (check with point of sharp knife). Let octopus cool in cooking water."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Discard cooked vegetables. Cut octopus into small pieces, and toss with olive oil, lemon juice, salt, pepper, pepper flakes and basil. Marinate, refrigerated, for 3 to 4 hours. Simmer potatoes in salted water until tender. Chop remaining raw vegetables."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Blanch carrots for about 5 minutes and onions for about 2 minutes, just to remove some of the crunch; shock in ice water to chill. Mix octopus with raw celeriac, cooked potatoes and blanched carrots and onions. Adjust seasoning, and then drizzle with fresh olive oil and lemon juice, if you like. Garnish with minced basil, and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 757.7, "protein_g": 42.9, "carbohydrates_g": 79.1, "fat_g": 30.4, "saturated_fat_g": 4.5, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 108.9, "sodium_mg": 1978.0, "fiber_g": 12.6, "sugar_g": 11.4, "unsaturated_fat_g": 24.0, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["greek"], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "carrot", "octopus", "red onion", "salad"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 10}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1999-09-08", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:01:42.809380+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "octopus-with-garlic-sauce", "nyt_id": 1781, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1781-octopus-with-garlic-sauce", "name": "Octopus With Garlic Sauce", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "Adapted from Aglaia Kremezi's \"Foods of the Greek Islands\"", "servings": {"text": "6 to 8 servings", "min": 6, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 40, "raw": {"total": "40 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 pounds cleaned fresh or unthawed frozen octopus", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "cleaned fresh or unthawed frozen octopus", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 cup caper potato-garlic dip (see recipe)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "caper potato-garlic dip (see recipe)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "If using fresh octopus, rinse it well and place in a heavy, nonreactive pot. Cook over medium heat, covered, for 10 minutes. Reduce the heat to low and simmer for 20 minutes, or until the octopus is fork-tender, adding a few tablespoons of water as needed. If using frozen octopus, place it in the pot still frozen and cook over medium-low heat, turning frequently, until thawed. Remove from heat."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Drain the octopus, reserving the cooking liquid, and cut it into bite-size pieces. Place in a serving bowl. Stir in a few tablespoons of the cooking liquid to thin the dip to sauce consistency. Pour over the octopus and cool to room temperature. Garnish with reserved capers and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 107.4, "protein_g": 17.3, "carbohydrates_g": 5.8, "fat_g": 1.2, "saturated_fat_g": 0.3, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 54.4, "sodium_mg": 261.9, "fiber_g": 0.4, "sugar_g": 0.2, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.5, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["greek"], "diet": [], "course": ["appetizer"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["dips and spreads", "five ingredient", "garlic", "octopus", "saute"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 3.0, "count": 31}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2000-12-10", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T03:50:40.977007+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
